<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#speechThoughtIntegratedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text representing character dialogue, thoughts, or internal communication in memes"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01269#toxicity_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme uses Kermit the Frog, a non-Muslim fictional character, to mock or dismiss Muslims by explicitly stating 'definitely not a Muslim'. This leverages a harmful stereotype that reduces a religious group to a caricature, potentially reinforcing prejudice and discrimination against Muslims. The intent is to ridicule or belittle Muslims by juxtaposing them with a popular cartoon character, which can be seen as a form of cultural or religious mockery."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01269#meme_format> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relatedTo> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01269#kermit_waving_scene> .
