<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01269#assertion_about_01269> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#hasToxicityExplanation> "The meme uses Kermit the Frog, a non-Muslim fictional character, to mock or dismiss Muslims by explicitly stating 'definitely not a Muslim'. This leverages a harmful stereotype that reduces a religious group to a caricature, potentially reinforcing prejudice and discrimination against Muslims. The intent is to ridicule or belittle Muslims by juxtaposing them with a popular cartoon character, which can be seen as a form of cultural or religious mockery."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#environmentallyTextualIn> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecated> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
_:neaa3726a7ba34412820b871e80d4a10ab31 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
