<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01269#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: kermit_the_frog_definitely_not_a_muslim; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features Kermit the Frog, a well-known fictional character, with the text overlay 'definitely not a muslim'. This meme uses juxtaposition to mock or dismiss the idea of Muslims by associating them with a non-Muslim character. While Kermit is a fictional character, the meme leverages his widely recognized image to make a derogatory statement about Muslims, implying they are not 'real' or 'authentic' in some way. This can be considered harmful as it contributes to the dehumanization and stereotyping of a religious group, potentially reinforcing prejudice and discrimination. The meme does not target an individual but rather a community based on religion, which falls under harmful content as it can incite bias and negative attitudes toward Muslims. The intent is to ridicule or belittle Muslims by using a popular cartoon character as a contrast, which can be seen as a form of cultural or religious mockery."@en .
